Fingerprint 0354: the overlay only on the lock screen and in a capture; QUP1 hw-gated AHB clocks + BCM QUP1 vote.
Owner (2026-10-27): "what is this fingerprint-reader overlay on the display while it is not connected to the
fingerprint at all" / "fingerprint should only show on the lockscreen and not always, and the overlay has to be
subtle, not a white thing". 0351 drew the white disc on every frame from boot (negronifp_hl=2 in the everything
boot-args) and made every GPU frame wait on its copy fence.

NegroniFramebuffer.cpp: negronifp_hl=1|2 (default 0) now only ALLOWS the overlay. What is shown
(negroni_fp_hl_show): 0 nothing; 1 the lock-screen glyph (two thin 2 px rings at r and 0.55 r in a fixed dim grey
0x505050, no blend, no fill, no HBM) while kern.negroni_fp_ui = 1; 2 the white disc of 0351 only while 0353's capture
window is open (negroni_fp_capture_window, 2 s safety timeout) AND a finger is inside the circle (negroni_touch.c
reports every finger to negroni_fp_touch). Drawn at each present (after the copy, as the badges) and at once on a
state change (negroni_fp_overlay_update: the lock screen presents no frame; the pixels under the direct drawing
are saved and put back when the overlay goes away, unless a present came in between; not while zero-copy is
active). One IOLock around every drawing and state change (sysctl, touch thread, fp_thread, work loop); the save
buffer and the lock are made once at the boot-arg parse. Fingers are tracked in every mode (the capture needs
them with negronifp_hl=0 too); only the drawing is gated. Presents are counted in present(). No fence wait in
presentFinish and no drawing when nothing is shown. Review fixes (Opus, 2026-10-27): F1 lock + one-time buffer,
F2 fingers in every mode, F3 fixed colour, F4 present counter + limits listed in the code comment. The HBM DCS set goes with 0353's
capture, not with the drawing; negronifp_hl=2 skips it (disc only). The boot-time "HBM once" callout of 0351 is gone.
negroni_fp.c: sysctl kern.negroni_fp_ui (0/1, root writes; userland/fp/negroni-fpd sets it from the SpringBoard
lock state); step 2: wrap_1 m_ahb/s_ahb in hardware clock gating mode (CBCR HW_CTL, CLK_OFF reads 1 while idle:
0x80000002 on the phone) are not checked, as Linux clk_branch_wait and 0334 for QUP2; RPMh BCM "QUP1" vote
(negroni_rpmh_qup_bcm of 0334, 5000 kBps, EBUSY retries; negronifp_bcm=0 skips, negronifp_bcm_kbps=N); step 11
waits negronifp_fingerwait s (default 10) for a finger inside the circle before HBM + disc (no finger: no HBM, no
disc, the protocol test runs anyway). Applies after 0334 and 0353.
Details: patches/xnu/README-fingerprint.md "0354", docs/notes.md.

